### ONE BLOCK RATHER THAN TWO, because these types are one phrase in two costumes and every rule
### below holds for both. A NEW PHRASE-BACKED TYPE APPENDS A LINE to the list immediately below and
### changes nothing else; a type with a `data` shape of its own opens its own block instead.
###
### Their rungs are text and nothing else:
###
###   missingvowels -> { "answer", "category"?, "displayed",
###                      "hints": [{ "text": "..." }, { "text": "..." }, { "text": "..." }] }
###   cryptogram    -> { "answer", "category"?, "ciphertext",
###                      "hints": [{ "text": "..." }, { "text": "..." }, { "text": "..." }] }
###
### No `metadata` key at all on those -- absent, not null. A phrase rung is a sentence; there is no
### structure on it for a board to act on.
###
### `answer` ships for the same offline-first reason `acceptedSolutions` does.
###
### `category` is OMITTED, not null, wherever it is hidden -- hiding it is part of the difficulty.
### The table hides it at difficulties 3 AND 5 (generators/category-visibility.ts). TODAY ONLY
### DIFFICULTY 3 EVER LOSES IT ON THE WIRE, and the reason is the band sets rather than the table:
